/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Schuylkill County runs 75 years back to 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids September to October came in under 90% of normal in 36 of them. In 2025, August to September came in at 43% of normal on the middle of the grids, and May to June at 179%. Grid 25115 had its driest year in 1980 at 64% of normal. On grid 24816, the preliminary estimate for July to August 2026 is 83.7.</p>"}
